01:01:14.074 --> 01:01:18.074
On this mountain the Lord will provide.

244
01:01:18.074 --> 01:01:20.074
And I love it.

245
01:01:22.074 --> 01:01:24.074
And I am very happy with this.

246
01:01:25.074 --> 01:01:27.074
It is more than enough.

247
01:01:27.074 --> 01:01:31.074
On this mountain the Lord will provide.

248
01:01:31.074 --> 01:01:33.074
Don't cry.

249
01:01:35.074 --> 01:01:46.074
In the coming year we will look at a number of things about how jam-packed with wonderful things this chapter is.

250
01:01:46.074 --> 01:01:50.074
This chapter is full of revelations.

251
01:01:50.074 --> 01:01:58.074
This chapter is amazing to apply to your personal life, for us as a church.

252
01:01:58.074 --> 01:02:02.074
First, I want to take you to verse 2.

253
01:02:02.074 --> 01:02:10.074
I don't have much time today, because I want to explain something else as a piece of vision, a work we are engaged in as a church.

254
01:02:10.074 --> 01:02:14.074
But don't worry, because we still have a whole year. Amen.

255
01:02:15.074 --> 01:02:23.074
I will only give you the simple bullet points as an outline of what I mean,

256
01:02:23.074 --> 01:02:29.074
and what we as a church are going through when we say, On this mountain the Lord will provide.

257
01:02:29.074 --> 01:02:34.074
On the mountain of the Lord, the Lord will give what is needed.

258
01:02:34.074 --> 01:02:39.074
On the mountain of the Lord, the Lord will give what is needed.

259
01:02:39.074 --> 01:02:47.074
Bullet point 1, what I want to highlight from the theme of this year, is the mountain of the Lord.

260
01:02:47.074 --> 01:02:58.074
So if you are taking notes, you can simply write down that one of the keywords of this theme is the mountain of the Lord.

261
01:02:58.074 --> 01:03:04.074
Mountains are significant when you look at the Word of God.

262
01:03:04.074 --> 01:03:12.074
Mountains mean not only for us when we come from the camps where no mountain can be found, by the way.

263
01:03:12.074 --> 01:03:18.074
If it is a mountain, then it is one from a vacation shop, but for the rest, no mountain can be found here.

264
01:03:18.074 --> 01:03:29.074
But when we go on vacation and you drive through the Swiss mountain landscapes,

265
01:03:29.074 --> 01:03:34.074
then you have a wow effect, right?

266
01:03:34.074 --> 01:03:42.074
When I see the mountains, I can only say, wow what a God we have.

267
01:03:42.074 --> 01:03:49.074
For he makes the mountains because he loves it, because he is great.

268
01:03:49.074 --> 01:03:54.074
And that wow effect he has placed in us.

269
01:03:54.074 --> 01:04:00.074
Pay close attention, all wow effects God has placed in us.

270
01:04:00.074 --> 01:04:08.074
He made us to be able to say wow, so that we can say wow to him with our wow.

271
01:04:08.074 --> 01:04:11.074
We just read this in Psalm 65.

272
01:04:11.074 --> 01:04:19.074
The earth is filled with people who say wow about who God is and what he has made.

273
01:04:19.074 --> 01:04:23.074
So our first task is to behold him.

274
01:04:23.074 --> 01:04:28.074
Mountains have always been in God's Word, and we will go through this this year,

275
01:04:28.074 --> 01:04:35.074
mountains always stand as a symbol guaranteed for the glory of God

276
01:04:35.074 --> 01:04:44.074
and for the revelation of what God does, who he is, and what he brings.

277
01:04:44.074 --> 01:04:50.074
So we have here Genesis 22. God provides on a mountain.

278
01:04:50.074 --> 01:05:01.074
We have the story where Moses sees that he is initially depressed and aimless in his life.

279
01:05:01.074 --> 01:05:08.074
At one point, he ends up in the desert, but he sees on a mountain a burning bush.

280
01:05:08.074 --> 01:05:13.074
And he goes up to have a meeting with God on a mountain.

281
01:05:13.074 --> 01:05:19.074
A little further you see that on a mountain the law of God is given to Moses.

282
01:05:19.074 --> 01:05:23.074
It is on a mountain where all these encounters take place.

283
01:05:23.074 --> 01:05:32.074
What many people do not know is that the Garden of Eden, the garden you read about in the Old Testament in Genesis 1,

284
01:05:32.074 --> 01:05:35.074
the Garden of Eden was not just a garden, it was also a mountain.

285
01:05:35.074 --> 01:05:40.074
It was a place where God and man had intimacy with each other.

286
01:05:40.074 --> 01:05:44.074
This was the place, the perfect place that represents heaven.

287
01:05:44.074 --> 01:05:51.074
It was a mountain of encounter, it is a mountain of being together with the Most High.

288
01:05:52.074 --> 01:05:56.074
It is on a mountain where your and my Lord was crucified.

289
01:05:56.074 --> 01:06:00.074
It was on a mountain where he paid for your and my sin.

290
01:06:00.074 --> 01:06:08.074
It was on a mountain where he set his foot and said, on this mountain I will build my church.

291
01:06:08.074 --> 01:06:11.074
And the gates of hell will not prevail against it.

292
01:06:11.074 --> 01:06:16.074
It is from that mountain that Jesus sends out his disciples,

293
01:06:16.074 --> 01:06:21.074
sending the disciples out to take authority over the earth.

294
01:06:21.074 --> 01:06:26.074
It is from a mountain that Jesus says, I send you 70 disciples

295
01:06:26.074 --> 01:06:31.074
to heal the blind, to heal the deaf, to cast out demons.

296
01:06:31.074 --> 01:06:37.074
I give you from this mountain my authority, says Jesus,

297
01:06:37.074 --> 01:06:43.074
to bring the world back to the creation order of the mountain of Eden.

298
01:06:43.074 --> 01:06:47.074
So the mountain of Eden, that is where it ultimately goes wrong.

299
01:06:47.074 --> 01:06:50.074
Then you see that there is a destruction in our creation.

300
01:06:50.074 --> 01:06:55.074
And then ultimately you see that Jesus takes back the authority.

301
01:06:55.074 --> 01:06:58.074
and he says, on this mountain I will build my church.

302
01:06:58.074 --> 01:07:04.074
And from this mountain I will show you what my plan is for this creation, in Jesus' name.

303
01:07:04.074 --> 01:07:06.074
Hallelujah.

304
01:07:06.074 --> 01:07:09.074
Oh, we are going to experience so much more about mountains.

305
01:07:09.074 --> 01:07:12.074
Mountains, mountains, mountains. Hallelujah.

306
01:07:12.074 --> 01:07:16.074
But there is something else that has to do with mountains.

307
01:07:16.074 --> 01:07:23.074
There is another important aspect that mountains represent as a symbol.

308
01:07:23.074 --> 01:07:28.074
Mountains are not just a meeting of God to humanity.

309
01:07:28.074 --> 01:07:34.074
Mountains are not just a place where God gives revelations to humanity.

310
01:07:34.074 --> 01:07:37.074
Mountains are also places of worship.

311
01:07:38.074 --> 01:07:43.074
Mountains represent worship.

312
01:07:43.074 --> 01:07:47.074
Mountains represent dedication.

313
01:07:47.074 --> 01:07:51.074
Mountains are places where the people...

314
01:07:51.074 --> 01:07:56.074
So you should not look at this only from our Western modern culture.

315
01:07:56.074 --> 01:07:59.074
You take a cable car and you stand at the top of the mountain.

316
01:07:59.074 --> 01:08:00.074
Oh, nice, that's it.

317
01:08:00.074 --> 01:08:07.074
No, mountains have, from ancient times and from the Jewish Scripture that you read...

318
01:08:07.074 --> 01:08:11.074
Mountains represent a significant...

319
01:08:11.074 --> 01:08:19.074
They require a sacrifice to come up from a place where the people are below.

320
01:08:19.074 --> 01:08:23.074
You should imagine it as an agricultural culture, for example.

321
01:08:23.074 --> 01:08:26.074
Or Bedouins who go through mountains and landscapes.

322
01:08:26.074 --> 01:08:31.074
Above that, the majesty and revelation of the Lord can be found.

323
01:08:31.074 --> 01:08:34.074
So someone who is devoted to the Creator...

324
01:08:34.074 --> 01:08:37.074
Someone who has a desire for God...

325
01:08:37.074 --> 01:08:41.074
That person goes from the place where ordinary people are...

326
01:08:41.074 --> 01:08:46.074
That person will lift themselves up and will bring a path upward...

327
01:08:46.074 --> 01:08:49.074
To have a meeting with God on the mountains.

328
01:08:49.074 --> 01:08:53.074
So mountains represent a place of worship.

329
01:08:54.074 --> 01:08:59.074
When Jesus is teaching the people about the love of the Father...

330
01:08:59.074 --> 01:09:00.074
Then Jesus is sometimes tired.

331
01:09:00.074 --> 01:09:02.074
Jesus was fully human.

332
01:09:02.074 --> 01:09:04.074
Jesus was not a superhuman.

333
01:09:04.074 --> 01:09:07.074
He was the true human.

334
01:09:07.074 --> 01:09:11.074
But he was a fully human just like you and me.

335
01:09:11.074 --> 01:09:13.074
Someone who was also tired.

336
01:09:13.074 --> 01:09:17.074
Someone who, after a day of teaching and a day of praying for people...

337
01:09:17.074 --> 01:09:19.074
Jesus was sometimes tired too.

338
01:09:19.074 --> 01:09:21.074
And what does the Word of God teach then?

339
01:09:21.074 --> 01:09:27.074
The Word of God teaches that Jesus withdrew to a mountain.

340
01:09:27.074 --> 01:09:33.074
To be alone with God all night on that mountain.

341
01:09:33.074 --> 01:09:36.074
For where did Jesus recharge himself?

342
01:09:36.074 --> 01:09:38.074
Where was his recharge?

343
01:09:38.074 --> 01:09:39.074
On a mountain.

344
01:09:39.074 --> 01:09:41.074
With the Father.

345
01:09:41.074 --> 01:09:47.074
And in 2023, Vanessa and I want to continue to nurture Open Church...

346
01:09:47.074 --> 01:09:53.074
And move forward and learn together what it is in 2023.

347
01:09:53.074 --> 01:09:56.074
To continue and to realize.

348
01:09:56.074 --> 01:10:00.074
2022 and even 2020.

349
01:10:00.074 --> 01:10:03.074
My house shall be a house of prayer.

350
01:10:03.074 --> 01:10:06.074
My house shall be a house of prayer.

351
01:10:06.074 --> 01:10:08.074
For do you know what it is church?

352
01:10:08.074 --> 01:10:13.074
We cannot be a church if we are not in worship with Him.

353
01:10:13.074 --> 01:10:17.074
We are not a church if we do not know how to pray.

354
01:10:17.074 --> 01:10:23.074
We are not a church if prayer is not our first commitment.

355
01:10:23.074 --> 01:10:29.074
For yes, if you know that the revelations of the Lord can be found on a mountain...

356
01:10:29.074 --> 01:10:37.074
And if you understand the mighty spiritual symbol of that mountain...

357
01:10:37.074 --> 01:10:41.074
And you understand that on the mountain the revelation can be received.

358
01:10:41.074 --> 01:10:44.074
On the mountain the provision of God can be received.

359
01:10:44.074 --> 01:10:49.074
If you can even have a personal encounter with God on the mountain.

360
01:10:49.074 --> 01:10:55.074
Moses and Elijah had personal encounters on mountains with God.

361
01:10:55.074 --> 01:11:01.074
But if you want that, then you must be willing to climb that mountain.

362
01:11:02.074 --> 01:11:07.074
Yes, then you must be willing to climb that mountain.

363
01:11:07.074 --> 01:11:11.074
I thought, Tim, that you just said, it is more than enough?

364
01:11:11.074 --> 01:11:15.074
I thought you just said, the cross is sufficient?

365
01:11:15.074 --> 01:11:17.074
Why then must I climb mountains?

366
01:11:17.074 --> 01:11:20.074
Immediately our flesh rises up.

367
01:11:20.074 --> 01:11:23.074
At least, I don't hear any hugs.

368
01:11:23.074 --> 01:11:29.074
Immediately, when God asks something of us in terms of sacrifices...

369
01:11:29.074 --> 01:11:33.074
Immediately when God says, I want a sacrifice from you.

370
01:11:33.074 --> 01:11:38.074
Then immediately our flesh says something like, yes but isn't it more than enough?

371
01:11:38.074 --> 01:11:42.074
Isn't it so? Isn't it over? I don't have to do anything more?

372
01:11:44.074 --> 01:11:48.074
Abraham was about to give his son.

373
01:11:48.074 --> 01:11:52.074
And this is for a law.

374
01:11:52.074 --> 01:11:55.074
Why do I say this? This is for a law.

375
01:11:55.074 --> 01:11:59.074
Because the law has made us guilty.

376
01:11:59.074 --> 01:12:04.074
And from that law, because we were guilty, God also came with a system of sacrifices...

377
01:12:04.074 --> 01:12:07.074
to free us from the sins we committed.

378
01:12:07.074 --> 01:12:13.074
But Abraham did not bring a sacrifice to God out of his sins, realize that.

379
01:12:13.074 --> 01:12:17.074
Abraham had no sins, realize that.

380
01:12:17.074 --> 01:12:21.074
Abraham came from a pagan society.

381
01:12:21.074 --> 01:12:24.074
Abraham came from a pagan society.

382
01:12:24.074 --> 01:12:27.074
Where everything was possible.

383
01:12:27.074 --> 01:12:31.074
And by the way, where child sacrifices were also quite normal.

384
01:12:33.074 --> 01:12:37.074
You have to imagine that if there is a good harvest...

385
01:12:38.074 --> 01:12:42.074
and you do not know the love of the Father intimately yourself.

386
01:12:42.074 --> 01:12:47.074
You are a farmer and you depend on a good harvest to survive.

387
01:12:47.074 --> 01:12:50.074
And a drought is coming.

388
01:12:50.074 --> 01:12:52.074
What do you think then?

389
01:12:52.074 --> 01:12:54.074
The gods must be angry.

390
01:12:54.074 --> 01:12:58.074
What are you going to do? Then you will bring an offering to the gods.

391
01:12:58.074 --> 01:13:01.074
Maybe there was a flood.

392
01:13:01.074 --> 01:13:06.074
Then the gods of the clouds, the gods of the rain, and the gods of the sea must be angry.

393
01:13:06.074 --> 01:13:11.074
What should you do then? Then you must give an offering to appease the gods.

394
01:13:11.074 --> 01:13:15.074
It is from such a society that God calls Abraham and says...

395
01:13:15.074 --> 01:13:21.074
Go away from Ur of the Chaldeans, for I am a very different god than what you think at this moment.

396
01:13:22.074 --> 01:13:26.074
And God calls Abraham away from a place...

397
01:13:26.074 --> 01:13:32.074
where occultism and where the worship of gods, whatever a god means...

398
01:13:32.074 --> 01:13:35.074
that was not at all who God really was.

399
01:13:35.074 --> 01:13:39.074
God calls Abraham away and says, I will take care of you.

400
01:13:39.074 --> 01:13:43.074
I am the God of heaven and earth. I love you.

401
01:13:43.074 --> 01:13:46.074
Come follow me and here comes the test.

402
01:13:46.074 --> 01:13:53.074
God tests Abraham by saying, give me your son.

403
01:13:53.074 --> 01:14:02.074
And many people think, okay, so the test is in the fact that Abraham would give his son.

404
01:14:02.074 --> 01:14:04.074
And that is correct.

405
01:14:04.074 --> 01:14:10.074
Only, there is something in the revelation that Abraham received from God.

406
01:14:10.074 --> 01:14:12.074
There is something much deeper.

407
01:14:12.074 --> 01:14:17.074
Abraham already had a revelation that God would provide.

408
01:14:17.074 --> 01:14:20.074
And therein lies the test of faith.

409
01:14:20.074 --> 01:14:26.074
The test of faith lies in the fact that Abraham knew what God was asking of him.

410
01:14:26.074 --> 01:14:31.074
But Abraham already had a revelation that God would provide.

411
01:14:31.074 --> 01:14:37.074
And if you know that God would provide and God says to you, but I want this offering...

412
01:14:37.074 --> 01:14:42.074
then it is until the very last moment that God says, would you really do it?

413
01:14:42.074 --> 01:14:46.074
And Abraham knows to himself, but he will provide.

414
01:14:46.074 --> 01:14:51.074
He says to his servant, we will come back after worship.

415
01:14:51.074 --> 01:14:54.074
A mountain represents worship.

416
01:14:54.074 --> 01:15:00.074
A mountain also represents bringing offerings to God to show how much you love God.

417
01:15:01.074 --> 01:15:07.074
Here is my presentation on what I would so much like to teach us as believing people.

418
01:15:07.074 --> 01:15:13.074
Even in 2023, God still asks for offerings from his people.

419
01:15:13.074 --> 01:15:17.074
Offerings are not atonement offerings.

420
01:15:17.074 --> 01:15:21.074
The cross is more than enough.

421
01:15:21.074 --> 01:15:26.074
So when we come to God to bring him an offering...

422
01:15:26.074 --> 01:15:30.074
we never do this to come into a better standing with him.

423
01:15:30.074 --> 01:15:34.074
We never come to God with our tithe to then say...

424
01:15:34.074 --> 01:15:38.074
look here Lord, for this is not why.

425
01:15:38.074 --> 01:15:43.074
We give our offerings to him because we love him.

426
01:15:43.074 --> 01:15:47.074
Because we want to show our love to him.

427
01:15:47.074 --> 01:15:53.074
Because we want to say, you are worth more to me than my little, little, little.

428
01:15:53.074 --> 01:15:59.074
When you fast, at the end of this month we are approaching a fasting period of 10 days.

429
01:15:59.074 --> 01:16:04.074
When you fast it is not because you fast to say...

430
01:16:04.074 --> 01:16:09.074
Lord, thank you for the cross, but I did something wrong yesterday.

431
01:16:09.074 --> 01:16:14.074
So if I now agree with you for 10 days that I will not eat anymore, is it then okay between us again?

432
01:16:14.074 --> 01:16:16.074
This is not why we fast.

433
01:16:16.074 --> 01:16:23.074
We fast because we say, you are so important to me, you are worth more to me than my food.

434
01:16:23.074 --> 01:16:25.074
You are worth more to me than my money.

435
01:16:25.074 --> 01:16:28.074
You are even worth more to me than my marriage.

436
01:16:28.074 --> 01:16:32.074
You are worth more to me than my child, what Abraham says here.

437
01:16:32.074 --> 01:16:35.074
And God who says, am I really worth that much?

438
01:16:35.074 --> 01:16:40.074
And Abraham says, you are worth everything to me.

439
01:16:40.074 --> 01:16:42.074
And God says, then give me your son.

440
01:16:42.074 --> 01:16:46.074
And we think, what a terrible question, why would God ask this?

441
01:16:46.074 --> 01:16:49.074
But I see the beauty of God here.

442
01:16:49.074 --> 01:16:52.074
Oh, what a wonderful question from God.

443
01:16:52.074 --> 01:17:00.074
Because in the Mesopotamian society, the time in which Abraham lived, children were continuously sacrificed.

444
01:17:00.074 --> 01:17:06.074
For the most bizarre, wooden, carved strange gods with odd noses and necks.

445
01:17:07.074 --> 01:17:12.074
And the people gave their children out of penance and out of fear.

446
01:17:12.074 --> 01:17:14.074
And God says, come with your child.

447
01:17:14.074 --> 01:17:18.074
And at the moment Abraham wants to do it, God says, stop.

448
01:17:18.074 --> 01:17:20.074
I am a different God.

449
01:17:20.074 --> 01:17:23.074
Stop, I am not a God who demands things from you.

450
01:17:23.074 --> 01:17:26.074
Stop, I am not a God who wants to make you afraid.

451
01:17:26.074 --> 01:17:31.074
Stop, I am not a God who takes pleasure in child sacrifices.

452
01:17:31.074 --> 01:17:35.074
Stop, I don't even like lambs and rams on your side.

453
01:17:35.074 --> 01:17:37.074
I am the one who provides.

454
01:17:37.074 --> 01:17:40.074
And this is the God we get to know on the mountain.

455
01:17:40.074 --> 01:17:43.074
God provides Himself.

456
01:17:43.074 --> 01:17:46.074
God is the one who provides Himself.

457
01:17:46.074 --> 01:17:48.074
This is so beautiful.

458
01:17:48.074 --> 01:17:51.074
And this is the revelation that Abraham had.

459
01:17:51.074 --> 01:17:53.074
Because when God, check it out.

460
01:17:53.074 --> 01:17:58.074
Because when God says to Abraham, Abraham, go away from this area.

461
01:17:58.074 --> 01:18:02.074
I want to guide you and I want to build a true friendship with you.

462
01:18:02.074 --> 01:18:04.074
I want to show you who I really am.

463
01:18:04.074 --> 01:18:13.074
Even if Abraham had the same image of God in the earlier days, why then go?

464
01:18:13.074 --> 01:18:18.074
So Abraham had a revelation of a better God.

465
01:18:18.074 --> 01:18:20.074
A true God.

466
01:18:20.074 --> 01:18:22.074
A God who loves you.

467
01:18:22.074 --> 01:18:24.074
A God who takes care of you.

468
01:18:24.074 --> 01:18:27.074
A God with whom you can make mistakes.

469
01:18:27.074 --> 01:18:29.074
You hear it?

470
01:18:29.074 --> 01:18:31.074
A God with whom you can make mistakes.

471
01:18:32.074 --> 01:18:35.074
Not a God with whom you may make mistakes.

472
01:18:35.074 --> 01:18:37.074
But it does happen.

473
01:18:37.074 --> 01:18:39.074
Abraham makes mistakes.

474
01:18:39.074 --> 01:18:41.074
Abraham does strange things.

475
01:18:41.074 --> 01:18:44.074
Abraham even lies.

476
01:18:44.074 --> 01:18:46.074
And does all sorts of strange things.

477
01:18:46.074 --> 01:18:48.074
To raise sons and so on.

478
01:18:48.074 --> 01:18:51.074
We will go into that later.

479
01:18:51.074 --> 01:18:54.074
But God guides him out of His love.

480
01:18:54.074 --> 01:18:59.074
